<!-- HAND-MAINTAINED since 2026-08-21. First written 2026-08-17 by a generator that
     is NOT in this repo: nothing under src/ emits this file, and searching for
     startingCountAtWorldCreation across every script finds only set_planet_subcount.py,
     which reads the field and never writes a patch. Edit it here, by hand, carefully.

     🔑 startingCountAtWorldCreation is the field that decides which factions a world
     generates. WorldGenerationData.ResetFactionCounts() repeats each ConfigurableFaction's
     defName that many times, so zeroing it removes the faction from the DEFAULT list.
     That is this file's whole job and it zeroes that field on 48 FactionDefs.

     🔴 IT NO LONGER TOUCHES maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation, and must not again. The
     header used to say that field "is only a cap and changes nothing on its own." THAT
     IS FALSE AT ZERO. FactionGenerator.ConfigurableFactions is
        from f in DefDatabase<FactionDef>.AllDefs where f.maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation > 0
     and Page_CreateWorldParams builds the Configure Factions page from that enumeration
     === so at 0 the row is not capped, it is DELETED, and the owner cannot add the
     faction back at the screen. Four rows WORLDGEN_FACTION_CHECKLIST.md tells him to
     tick were among them.
     ⚠️ requiredCountAtGameStart is not a safety net. FactionGenerator.InitializeFactions
     reads it ONLY where no faction list was configured; worldgen through the screen
     passes Current.CreatingWorld.info.factions and adds that list verbatim.

     🔴 EVERY op is wrapped in an OUTER PatchOperationConditional that tests whether the
     FactionDef exists at all, with NO <nomatch>. A PatchOperationConditional that matches
     nothing returns true and logs nothing, so a def belonging to a dropped mod - or living
     only in a mod's 1.4/1.5 folder and never loaded under 1.6 - is a SILENT no-op instead
     of a red error. Two earlier versions of this file threw 12 and 14 errors per load
     because they patched defs that were on disk but not in the game.

     KEPT configurable: our 14, plus the hidden/system factions the engine needs and every
     *Player* def. Regenerate after any mod-list change.
-->
<Patch>
  <!-- AA_BlackHive -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="AA_BlackHive"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>
        <li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
          <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="AA_BlackHive"]/startingCountAtWorldCreation</xpath>
          <match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
            <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="AA_BlackHive"]/startingCountAtWorldCreation</xpath>
            <value><startingCountAtWorldCreation>0</startingCountAtWorldCreation></value>
          </match>
          <nomatch Class="PatchOperationAdd">
            <xpath>/Defs/FactionDef[defName="AA_BlackHive"]</xpath>
            <value><startingCountAtWorldCreation>0</startingCountAtWorldCreation></value>
          </nomatch>
        </li>
      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>
